Hmm... maybe this idea needs to be combined with a new item:

Markers

As tin whistles are to magic whistles, ordinary markers are to magic
markers.

Ordinary markers can be used for everything magic markers are used for
except scribing scrolls.  Primarily, this means one could use them to
write Elbereth, or anything else one might want, on the floor.  They
have charges and can be refilled (indefinitely) with ink.

When a magic marker runs out of charges, it can be recharged once with
a scroll of charging or a potion of ink.  The second time it runs out,
it becomes an ordinary marker.  A potion of ink will make it into an
ordinary marker.  Scrolls of charging don't work on ordinary markers.

Potions of ink should be semi-rare items, considering their utility in
charging magic markers.  This would allow more Scrolls of Charging,
which are among the most useful scrolls, to be used for wands.

